WEBVTT

00:02.410 --> 00:05.380
In matters relating
to the world of the dead

00:05.480 --> 00:08.840
there is an institution that judges
the sins of the deceased

00:09.100 --> 00:10.640
the Ju-Oh-Cho.

00:11.480 --> 00:13.250
The Summons Section
of the Judgment Bureau

00:13.350 --> 00:17.080
comprises a group supporting
the ministry's operating functions

00:17.190 --> 00:20.020
by guiding the lost souls
that wander the mortal world.

00:20.390 --> 00:22.020
They are also known as...

00:22.260 --> 00:24.700
the Shinigami.

00:24.960 --> 00:31.630
nureta hitomi no oku

00:24.960 --> 00:31.630
Deep behind its wavering stare

00:33.340 --> 00:43.650
aoi tsuki wa shizuka ni koboreochiteyuku

00:33.340 --> 00:43.650
The pale moon quietly descends

00:33.420 --> 00:42.670
Yami no Matsuei

00:49.960 --> 00:55.830
azayaka na sekai wa

00:49.960 --> 00:55.830
The splendid world

00:58.200 --> 01:08.270
oto mo naku shizuka ni yami ni kieteyuku

00:58.200 --> 01:08.270
Disappears into the darkness without a sound

01:08.370 --> 01:16.010
byouyomi no naka kakemeguru yami no naka o

01:08.370 --> 01:16.010
Running about in the dark as time runs out

01:16.110 --> 01:22.640
soshite aratanaru toki o mukae ima

01:16.110 --> 01:22.640
A new era beckons now

01:25.360 --> 01:30.450
kizutsuita kuroi tsubasa

01:25.360 --> 01:30.450
The injured black wings

01:30.630 --> 01:37.000
tsuki no akari ni terasarete

01:30.630 --> 01:37.000
Shine in the moonlight

01:37.600 --> 01:41.800
utsukushiku maiagare

01:37.600 --> 01:41.800
Rising upward in a beautiful dance

01:41.940 --> 01:47.140
shinku no kuchizuke ga ima

01:41.940 --> 01:47.140
The crimson kiss

01:47.250 --> 01:54.080
kokoro no oku ni nagarekomu

01:47.250 --> 01:54.080
Flows deeply into the soul

01:54.250 --> 02:00.050
soshite yume no naka e

01:54.250 --> 02:00.050
Penetrating into one's dreams

02:22.380 --> 02:27.010
The one I love...
Come and find me quickly.

02:28.350 --> 02:33.360
Episode 10: The Kyoto Arc, Part 1

02:43.170 --> 02:46.290
You'll catch cold if you nap here.

02:50.940 --> 02:54.470
Like a small boat drifting in a sunset calm.

02:54.580 --> 02:57.480
Cherry blossoms bloom here all year round.

02:57.580 --> 02:59.710
How spoiled we are.

02:59.820 --> 03:01.080
Do you think so?

03:02.890 --> 03:07.120
It's the fleeting nature of the
blossoms that make them beautiful.

03:07.220 --> 03:08.950
And people too.

03:11.690 --> 03:14.690
Never mind. We've got a
meeting coming up, don't we?

03:15.200 --> 03:16.290
Tsuzuki-san...

03:23.010 --> 03:25.000
This is the first victim.

03:25.140 --> 03:27.470
The second, third...

03:27.580 --> 03:31.770
The fourth, and all the way up to the tenth.

03:31.880 --> 03:34.820
Serial murders that have
been taking place in Kyoto.

03:34.920 --> 03:38.820
The victims have all had their hair cut.

03:41.160 --> 03:44.130
There you have it. Tsuzuki, Kurosaki...

03:44.230 --> 03:46.690
I want you to fly to Kyoto
and help Watari on this.

03:46.800 --> 03:48.390
Uh, sure.

03:48.500 --> 03:50.160
I understand.

03:52.000 --> 03:55.200
It doesn't surprise me that this is
the spot for school field trips.

03:55.220 --> 03:57.860
Look at the number of students.

03:58.570 --> 04:03.200
Beautiful fall foliage here.
And great climate this time of year.

04:03.310 --> 04:07.340
I was born in Kyoto, so you can
leave the navigating to me.

04:07.950 --> 04:10.920
Also, this is a bountiful
season for local delicacies.

04:11.020 --> 04:13.820
Kyoto radishes, shrimp potatoes,
and mibuna cabbages...

04:13.920 --> 04:16.760
Oh, right. We can't forget
the matsutake mushrooms.

04:16.860 --> 04:20.020
Huh? Watari-san, I thought you were from Osaka.

04:20.130 --> 04:24.360
I was raised in Osaka, but I was born in Kyoto.

04:24.470 --> 04:28.460
Thanks to all that,
I've got an inaccurate Kansai accent.

04:28.570 --> 04:31.940
Watari, let's get down to business.

04:32.640 --> 04:35.580
What's the real reason why
you brought us here?

04:35.680 --> 04:38.010
You're responsible for this area.

04:38.110 --> 04:42.410
I'm sure there's a good reason for
you to bring us into your territory.

04:43.150 --> 04:45.250
You see through everything, Tsuzuki?

04:45.350 --> 04:47.720
All right.
I'll come right out with it.

04:47.820 --> 04:50.050
I wanted you to come take a look at this.

04:50.160 --> 04:51.320
Hair?

04:51.430 --> 04:54.400
The female murder victim was
clutching this in her hand.

04:54.500 --> 04:56.490
You think it's the culprit's hair?

04:56.600 --> 05:00.560
There's a good chance of it.
Ever seen anything like it?

05:01.670 --> 05:04.700
Silver hair like platinum blond...

05:10.250 --> 05:11.800
Could it be Muraki's?

05:23.360 --> 05:25.260
I'm sorry to disturb you.

05:27.060 --> 05:29.000
Where would Dr. Satomi be?

05:29.100 --> 05:30.760
Uh, yes. Satomi's...

05:30.870 --> 05:33.840
I mean Dr. Satomi's laboratory
is in the East Building.

05:34.170 --> 05:35.140
Thank you.

05:39.440 --> 05:40.770
What a beautiful man.

05:40.880 --> 05:44.870
He's like a doll. He has smoother skin than a woman's.

05:44.980 --> 05:46.740
His voice is so cool!

05:46.850 --> 05:49.820
How could Satomi know
such a wonderful man?

05:49.920 --> 05:53.360
Maybe he's a clone that
the doctor developed.

05:53.460 --> 05:55.550
Even so, he's gorgeous!

05:58.230 --> 06:00.650
Library

06:02.260 --> 06:03.560
Locked and secure.

06:04.000 --> 06:05.400
Wow, it's so dark.

06:05.500 --> 06:07.770
It took awhile to put those books back.

06:08.040 --> 06:10.160
It feels like a ghost is going to appear.

06:10.270 --> 06:11.830
Creepy, creepy...

06:11.940 --> 06:14.170
M-Maki, stop that.

06:14.280 --> 06:17.070
You're such a wimp, Mariko.

06:20.220 --> 06:21.910
Did you know?

06:22.280 --> 06:26.410
I've heard that they're secretly
developing a human clone here.

06:26.620 --> 06:28.590
N-No way.
That's just a stupid rumor.

06:28.690 --> 06:29.850
I suppose.

06:30.060 --> 06:32.530
But wouldn't it be nice
to have your own clone?

06:32.630 --> 06:35.620
She could go to school for me,
and I could just take it easy.

06:35.730 --> 06:39.500
But that would be a kind of waste of technology.

06:43.670 --> 06:45.300
H-Hey, wait up!

07:10.270 --> 07:12.460
Finally gave out, huh?

07:12.940 --> 07:15.870
No! I'm going to need more specimens!

07:15.970 --> 07:18.060
Strong specimens!

07:28.850 --> 07:31.750
You sure are quite something.

07:32.690 --> 07:35.750
Think about my situation.
I have to clean up after you.

07:41.900 --> 07:45.160
Just how many do you think there've been so far?

07:48.400 --> 07:51.070
I'd say there've been nine.

07:51.810 --> 07:54.640
The tea water has splashed a little, Oriya.

07:54.740 --> 07:57.680
Of course.
And actually there've been ten.

07:57.780 --> 07:59.440
I apologize.

07:59.550 --> 08:01.850
But, with your power,
it's nothing you can't handle.

08:03.090 --> 08:06.280
On the outside, Kokakurou is
an elite traditional restaurant.

08:06.820 --> 08:08.550
But inside...

08:08.660 --> 08:13.060
it's a secret harem for VIP's
in business and politics.

08:14.330 --> 08:16.230
And you run the place.

08:16.330 --> 08:20.200
With your connections,
I'm sure you can get them to bury it.

08:20.700 --> 08:24.500
- That may be so, but...
- I appreciate it.

08:24.610 --> 08:27.670
Geez... A hell of a friend you are.

08:34.120 --> 08:37.750
Come to think of it, the police
apparently found hair

08:37.850 --> 08:40.320
that's thought to
belong to the murderer.

08:40.590 --> 08:43.890
Fine and silky, platinum blonde
hair with a touch of silver?

08:43.990 --> 08:46.020
Geez... I wonder who it could be.

08:46.130 --> 08:49.930
You sure can be bold.
Are you sure you're okay?

08:50.700 --> 08:53.690
I'm not the kind of idiot
who'd get caught by the police.

08:53.800 --> 08:55.830
That was just a sign.

08:56.370 --> 08:57.340
Sign?

08:57.440 --> 08:58.570
Yes.

08:58.770 --> 09:02.770
For the one I love.
So he can find me quickly.

09:07.320 --> 09:10.180
- Watari, how much further?
- Just a bit more.

09:10.590 --> 09:13.450
Where are we staying?
A business hotel?

09:13.560 --> 09:16.520
If we're in Kyoto, we should stay
at some old inn with character.

09:16.630 --> 09:19.030
I can't wait to take a bath
as soon as I get there.

09:19.130 --> 09:21.820
Hisoka, I'll wash your back for you.

09:21.930 --> 09:26.230
You go ahead. I prefer to
take a nice long bath by myself.

09:26.670 --> 09:28.190
You're no fun.

09:28.300 --> 09:31.800
Were there any hotels or inns in this area?

09:34.710 --> 09:36.910
It looks like this is it.

09:37.580 --> 09:38.880
Where?

09:41.980 --> 09:43.880
Are you serious?

09:45.550 --> 09:48.250
That Tatsumi's such a cheapskate!

09:55.760 --> 09:57.360
When we do a DNA analysis

09:57.470 --> 10:00.800
comparing the article he
left behind in Nagasaki

10:00.900 --> 10:04.130
with the hair the murder victim was clutching.

10:04.240 --> 10:05.830
This is the result.

10:07.540 --> 10:10.810
The DNA comes from the same person.

10:12.310 --> 10:13.540
Muraki!

10:13.650 --> 10:16.780
But it's hard to imagine
that a perfectionist like Muraki

10:16.890 --> 10:19.180
would leave evidence like that.

10:21.090 --> 10:22.350
Where'd Hisoka go?

10:22.460 --> 10:25.050
He's gone out to get dinner.

10:25.790 --> 10:29.200
How far did he go?

10:35.400 --> 10:37.500
Maybe I bought too much stuff.

10:37.610 --> 10:40.230
Well, Tsuzuki will eat up any leftovers.

11:03.870 --> 11:06.330
Well, well. It's you again.

11:07.140 --> 11:08.360
Muraki!

11:08.910 --> 11:13.500
Yami no Matsuei

11:22.180 --> 11:25.780
You certainly like to get in the way, don't you?

11:32.390 --> 11:34.090
Don't trip and fall.

11:34.200 --> 11:39.130
They say you'll die within three years
if you fall from those steps.

11:39.670 --> 11:43.260
Although you were already killed by me.

11:43.370 --> 11:45.810
What do you plan to do?

11:45.910 --> 11:48.210
You're in the way.
Step aside.

11:48.310 --> 11:49.740
Answer me, Muraki!

11:49.850 --> 11:51.900
I'm not obliged to answer you.

11:52.150 --> 11:53.240
What?!

11:53.350 --> 11:55.510
You're a pestering one, aren't you?

11:55.620 --> 11:58.920
You still bearing a grudge
about Princess Tsubaki?

12:04.490 --> 12:07.090
<i>Doctor, I love you.</i>

12:08.600 --> 12:11.530
She tells me she loves and wants me.

12:11.630 --> 12:13.660
Getting all wrapped up
in her silly delusions.

12:13.770 --> 12:16.500
My little toy who died
like a pathetic fool.

12:16.610 --> 12:18.230
Wh-Why, you!

12:22.680 --> 12:23.800
Such a simpleton...

12:23.910 --> 12:27.140
You fly off the handle so easily.
What a child you are.

12:27.250 --> 12:28.650
L-Let go!

12:28.750 --> 12:32.240
I guess I'm going to have to
give you another little lesson.

12:33.220 --> 12:36.850
That night was a beautiful night,
just like now.

12:36.960 --> 12:38.320
Stop it...

12:38.530 --> 12:39.760
Hisoka!

12:41.460 --> 12:42.660
T-Tsuzuki!

12:42.760 --> 12:44.700
It's been a while, Tsuzuki-san.

12:45.670 --> 12:46.660
Muraki...

12:47.140 --> 12:49.760
You probably have many questions.

12:49.870 --> 12:52.900
I'll take you to where we can talk.

12:53.010 --> 12:56.310
It's bedtime for the boy.
Now, go on.

12:59.410 --> 13:00.780
Hold it!

13:00.880 --> 13:03.480
- Leave this to me.
- It's a trap!

13:03.590 --> 13:06.280
I don't want to involve you in this anymore.

13:06.390 --> 13:07.360
Tsuzuki...

13:07.460 --> 13:09.120
Don't worry.

13:15.130 --> 13:16.960
I'm so glad, Tsuzuki-san.

13:17.070 --> 13:21.800
To think I get to spend a night
alone with you in the ancient capital.

13:26.710 --> 13:28.540
Oh? Don't you like the food?

13:28.980 --> 13:32.040
Muraki, you're the culprit, aren't you?

13:32.780 --> 13:34.110
That's right.

13:34.220 --> 13:37.710
I am the culprit responsible
for those serial murders.

13:37.820 --> 13:40.150
All in order to draw you to me.

13:40.260 --> 13:42.990
Why did you cut the victims' hair?

13:43.090 --> 13:45.530
I can't answer that question.

13:45.860 --> 13:46.950
Stop messing around!

13:50.530 --> 13:54.160
How rude of you, Tsuzuki-san.
To attack me so violently.

13:54.670 --> 13:55.900
L-Let go!

13:57.640 --> 14:00.570
I can just take you into the bedroom like this.

14:00.680 --> 14:02.230
Don't mess with me!

14:02.340 --> 14:04.010
What's your aim?!

14:04.110 --> 14:07.010
Don't involve innocent people anymore!

14:07.120 --> 14:10.710
You are so truly kind.
You are so adorable.

14:11.820 --> 14:14.690
I may have to destroy you
because I love you so much.

14:14.790 --> 14:17.550
After piling up a few corpses before you.

14:17.660 --> 14:19.350
Cut this out!

14:21.600 --> 14:23.560
Oh, Tsuzuki-san...

14:23.670 --> 14:26.130
I see you wear your watch on your right wrist.

14:26.230 --> 14:28.130
Is that because you're a lefty?

14:28.240 --> 14:32.140
Or is it to hide the scars on your wrist?

14:39.750 --> 14:43.620
The curtain was raised with our
auspicious reunification in Nagasaki.

14:43.720 --> 14:46.620
We're coming up to
the climax of this drama.

14:46.720 --> 14:49.660
The time for you to take the stage is soon.

14:55.140 --> 14:57.100
Kokakurou

15:03.110 --> 15:06.670
<i>January 1st, 1925.</i>

15:06.780 --> 15:09.570
<i>This is my eighth new years
with that patient of mine.</i>

15:09.680 --> 15:13.080
<i>During that time, the patient
has taken no water, nor food.</i>

15:13.180 --> 15:15.450
<i>I can only explain it as a miracle.</i>

15:15.550 --> 15:20.110
<i>January 5th. The patient attempts
his first suicide of the year.</i>

15:20.220 --> 15:23.890
<i>The wound on his wrist would've
been fatal for a normal patient.</i>

15:23.990 --> 15:27.450
<i>But his remarkable ability to
recover has saved him again.</i>

15:27.560 --> 15:30.900
<i>His recovery was, however,
slow compared to previous times.</i>

15:31.000 --> 15:35.300
<i>January 12th.
The patient falls into a coma.</i>

15:35.400 --> 15:38.800
<i>His pupils are dilated.
His condition is deteriorating.</i>

15:38.910 --> 15:41.240
<i>January 20th. It's snowed.</i>

15:41.340 --> 15:43.370
<i>It's his ninth day in a coma.</i>

15:43.480 --> 15:46.740
<i>He regains consciousness
for a moment and commits suicide.</i>

15:46.850 --> 15:49.940
<i>Attempts to revive him do not succeed.</i>

15:51.550 --> 15:55.790
<i>Grandfather, your patient
will be returning soon.</i>

15:58.530 --> 15:59.960
<i>Soon.</i>

16:06.100 --> 16:08.830
Mariko, could you take this to Dr. Satomi?

16:09.970 --> 16:12.770
I completely forgot that he ordered this.

16:12.870 --> 16:15.340
I can't get away right now.
Please?

16:15.610 --> 16:17.770
Sure. Dr. Satomi, right?

16:27.260 --> 16:32.190
Oh, why does the school have
to be so creepy at night?

16:40.470 --> 16:42.060
What a beautiful man!

16:42.170 --> 16:44.700
I wonder if he teaches
at this university.

16:44.810 --> 16:48.000
Excuse me, young lady,
where would Dr. Satomi be?

16:48.110 --> 16:51.770
Uh, well, I'm just a student
from an affiliated school, so...

16:51.880 --> 16:53.440
Muraki-kun!

16:53.550 --> 16:55.180
Sorry to make you wait.

16:55.420 --> 16:56.480
And you are?

16:56.590 --> 16:59.450
Oh, this is the book you were looking for.

17:00.320 --> 17:03.220
Thanks for all the trouble.

17:05.490 --> 17:08.720
It's getting late.
Careful on your way home.

17:08.930 --> 17:11.400
Yes, sir! Excuse me!

17:12.900 --> 17:16.530
Muraki-san, huh?
I wonder if he's an assistant.

17:17.010 --> 17:21.640
Come to think of it, Dr. Satomi's
main specialty is genetic cloning.

17:21.740 --> 17:22.710
<i>Did you know?</i>

17:22.810 --> 17:26.940
<i>I've heard that they're secretly
developing a human clone here.</i>

17:27.450 --> 17:32.150
Could Muraki-san be the result of
Dr. Satomi's illegal experiments?

17:32.650 --> 17:35.680
Yeah, right. I've been reading
too many weird novels.

17:35.790 --> 17:38.120
I'm totally addicted to books.

17:38.860 --> 17:41.350
I really appreciate your help.

17:41.630 --> 17:45.360
Not only do you help me with
this distasteful research

17:45.470 --> 17:47.560
you've even arranged funding for me.

17:47.670 --> 17:52.130
It's only natural for an admiring
student to cooperate with his teacher.

17:52.240 --> 17:53.830
Muraki-kun...

17:56.710 --> 17:57.910
How shameful.

17:58.010 --> 18:00.850
Cell division has ceased again this time.

18:00.950 --> 18:03.850
I'm sorry, but I'll be needing another specimen.

18:03.950 --> 18:05.510
I see.

18:05.620 --> 18:08.250
Actually, I want you to look at this.

18:09.790 --> 18:12.260
It's an awfully old picture.

18:12.360 --> 18:16.060
I found it among my grandfather's
pile of old pictures.

18:16.160 --> 18:20.620
It's dated 1925...
The first year of the Showa Period.

18:20.940 --> 18:22.200
You may know this

18:22.300 --> 18:25.140
but we've been doctors
for generations in my family.

18:25.240 --> 18:28.640
My grandfather even had part of
the mansion turned into a hospital.

18:28.740 --> 18:31.370
I hear he had quite a good reputation.

18:32.180 --> 18:36.120
My grandfather had many friends
in the government and the army.

18:36.220 --> 18:40.120
Did you know that he was
even privy to state secrets?

18:40.220 --> 18:41.850
State secrets?

18:41.960 --> 18:44.250
That man in the picture.

18:44.360 --> 18:47.520
He was a patient at my grandfather's hospital.

18:48.300 --> 18:50.090
My grandfather, without hesitation

18:50.200 --> 18:54.290
let the penniless patient stay for eight years.

18:54.400 --> 18:55.990
Do you know why?

18:56.470 --> 19:00.530
Without eating or drinking,
and with no sleep at all

19:00.640 --> 19:02.770
he lived for eight years.

19:02.880 --> 19:04.240
What?!

19:10.320 --> 19:12.250
I've never heard of such nonsense!

19:12.350 --> 19:15.020
But he continued to live.

19:15.120 --> 19:18.320
Moreover, his body
did not deteriorate at all

19:18.430 --> 19:22.260
during his stay at the hospital
until he died at the age of 26.

19:22.360 --> 19:23.800
You mean he didn't age?

19:23.900 --> 19:25.490
How about it, Doctor?

19:25.600 --> 19:28.430
Don't you think he'd make a wonderful specimen?

19:28.540 --> 19:31.270
I think he might be very useful in your research.

19:34.010 --> 19:37.470
But I suppose he's no longer alive.

19:37.580 --> 19:40.740
- No. He's still alive.
- What?!

19:40.850 --> 19:44.310
I've searched many years
and have finally met him.

19:44.420 --> 19:47.180
He looks exactly as he does in the picture.

19:47.520 --> 19:51.960
Still the beautiful figure that he
was when he committed suicide

19:52.060 --> 19:54.860
on that snowy night 72 years ago.

20:05.210 --> 20:08.070
Muraki's the cause of all of this mayhem

20:08.180 --> 20:10.580
just to get a hold of me.

20:11.580 --> 20:14.280
Dragging in innocent people...

20:17.750 --> 20:19.380
All this time...

20:19.490 --> 20:23.750
many people have died because of me.

20:25.330 --> 20:26.420
Tsuzuki...

21:14.810 --> 21:17.400
How are you feeling, Saki?

21:19.080 --> 21:21.610
It's dark and cold in there.

21:21.980 --> 21:26.080
Soon you will have your own body.

21:27.220 --> 21:29.190
That's when...

21:29.620 --> 21:32.960
you will really die, Saki!

21:40.460 --> 21:43.510
Next Episode

21:43.510 --> 21:47.940
Muraki launched his final
plan in the ancient capital.

21:48.040 --> 21:52.170
Clone research?
What is that man up to?!

21:52.280 --> 21:55.680
Muraki! Am I not the one you're after?!

21:55.780 --> 21:58.150
Keep the innocent people out of this!

22:00.900 --> 22:10.410
Episode 11   The Kyoto Arc, Part 2

22:00.920 --> 22:04.450
Next time on Yami no Matsuei: The Kyoto Arc, Part 2.

22:05.830 --> 22:09.630
Those who live in the darkness wander aimlessly.

22:18.710 --> 22:22.070
arumikan no marui en o mashikaku ni orinagara

22:18.710 --> 22:22.070
As I square the round edges on the drink

22:22.180 --> 22:25.110
kimi o matsu machikado sa

22:22.180 --> 22:25.110
I wait for you on the street corner

22:25.210 --> 22:28.700
nakami no ekitai wa mou nurukute nomenai kedo

22:25.210 --> 22:28.700
The liquid inside is warm and I can't drink it anymore

22:28.820 --> 22:31.410
shikatanaku motsu ore sa

22:28.820 --> 22:31.410
But what can I do but hold onto to it?

22:31.520 --> 22:38.750
yami no naka de ore o utsusu
garasu keesu ni kazarareta

22:31.520 --> 22:38.750
In the glass case reflecting me in the darkness

22:38.860 --> 22:45.490
ningyou ga sakki kara kowai
kao de ore o miteru

22:38.860 --> 22:45.490
There is a doll that has been scowling at me

22:58.950 --> 23:05.370
ore no fuku kuchibue wa wari
to akarui uta de

22:58.950 --> 23:05.370
The tune I whistle is a bright and cheerful one

23:05.890 --> 23:11.820
zensekai no hitotachi ni
sasagerareta noizu

23:05.890 --> 23:11.820
A little noise dedicated to the people of the world

23:12.590 --> 23:18.930
dare hitori shiru hazu
no nai kono merodi ga

23:12.590 --> 23:18.930
No one could possibly recognize the melody

23:19.680 --> 23:25.080
omae ni wa kikoeru ka? Sayonara da
Love me

23:19.680 --> 23:25.080
But do you hear it?
Good-bye, Love me
